course: dictionary
lesson: 3951
title: One word, many shapes: funnel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A funnel is a tube that is wide at the top and narrow at the bottom. You use one to pour liquid or powder into a small opening without spilling. The shape of the word matches what it does: it guides things into a narrow place.
explain: Funnel can also be a verb. «Owls have a face that funnels sound into its ears.» The sound is not poured, but it is guided into a narrow place, so funnel means to move something through a narrow space. «The crowd was funnelled through the gate.» The people had to go through one at a time.
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. «Pour the juice through a funnel» is about a tube, but «a funnel cloud» is about a cloud. Read the words around the word, then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: A funnel is a tube that is wide at the top and narrow at the bottom.
fact: «Funnel» can also mean a chimney on a ship or steam train, where smoke comes out.
fact: A funnel cloud is the spinning, cone-shaped cloud of a tornado.
fact: To funnel means to move things or people through a narrow space.
fact: In «funnel-web spider», funnel is part of the spider's name, so it is not the same as the tube.
exercise: «Pour the juice through a funnel so none of it spills.» What is a funnel for? | *To pour liquid into a small opening without spilling | To hold a bird's nest | To cool the juice down quickly | To make a loud noise
exercise: «A funnel cloud swirled down from the dark sky.» What is a funnel cloud? | A cloud that brings snow | *A spinning, cone-shaped cloud of a tornado | A flat grey cloud with no shape | A soft white cloud that drifts slowly
exercise: «The owl's face funnels sound into its ears.» What does funnels mean here? | *Guides sound into a narrow place | Makes sound louder by shouting | Stops all sound from getting through | Turns sound into light
test: «The ship's funnel puffed black smoke into the sky.» What is a funnel on a ship? | *A chimney where the smoke comes out | A rope tied to the mast | A sail that catches the wind | A tube for pouring liquid
test: «The crowds were funnelled through the narrow gate, one at a time.» What does funnelled mean? | *Moved through a narrow space | Stopped completely at the wall | Shouted loudly at the gate | Pushed over a high fence
exam: «A funnel cloud is a sign of a tornado.» Which description fits a funnel cloud best? | A bright cloud that glows at night | A flat grey cloud that brings rain | A cloud made of tiny ice crystals | *A spinning, cone-shaped cloud, a sign of a tornado
